{
  "title": "C. C. Stern Foundry",
  "indexDescription": "C. C. Stern Type Foundry",
  "description": "C. C. Stern had a collection of printing equipment in Portland that became the core of the group that exists today. \n\nSeveral people interested in learning and maintaining the traditional printing methods bought a house in Clatskanie and set up shop there. \n\nThis printing tech was used for about 100 years before being replaced by desktop printing: Aldus PageMaker, Adobe Postscript and Apple laser writer in the 1990s. \n\nWe got involved when they decided to make broadsides for the poet laureates of Washington and Oregon. \n\nThey hosted us at the house for a reading in town. ",
